Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.80,0:00:02.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}What if the Moon disappeared?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.34,0:00:03.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.22,0:00:04.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Without a sound.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.93,0:00:06.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}You step outside.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.19,0:00:07.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}You look up.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.11,0:00:08.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}The sky is empty.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.35,0:00:10.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Just stars.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.03,0:00:11.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Then.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.32,0:00:12.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}One night.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.03,0:00:14.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Every night is now pitch black.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.24,0:00:15.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}No more moonlight.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.47,0:00:16.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Ever.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.85,0:00:17.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}One day.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.70,0:00:19.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}The oceans feel it first.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.31,0:00:21.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}The tides shrink to about one third.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.44,0:00:24.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Coastlines go strangely still.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.32,0:00:25.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}One month.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.20,0:00:28.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Corals that spawn by the full moon lose their signal.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.79,0:00:31.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Night hunters lose their light.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.02,0:00:32.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Millions of years.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.31,0:00:36.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Without the Moon holding it steady, Earth's tilt could start to wobble.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.89,0:00:39.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}The seasons could go wild.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.21,0:00:40.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}But here's the twist.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.73,0:00:42.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}The Moon is already leaving us.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.67,0:00:46.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}In nineteen sixty-nine, astronauts left mirrors on it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.19,0:00:48.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Scientists still fire lasers at them.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.48,0:00:52.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Every year, the Moon drifts about three point eight centimeters away.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.77,0:00:53.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}So remember.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.72,0:00:56.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Next time you see the Moon… look up.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.10,0:00:58.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}It won't stay this close forever.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.17,0:00:59.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Would you miss it?
